ank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T16:26:44-07:00","id":1545228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545042-favourite-adversaries?p=1545161#post1545161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but you can blast Pentex and Umbrella in the face with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you didn\u2019t blast Pentex in the face with magic really. You blasted a fictional versions of Blackwater Security (now known as Triple Canopy Inc. subsidiary of Apollo Global Management with a laundry list of various companies under their management that would make the Pentex board of directors need a change of pants) mercenaries and then celebrated your victory over the Wyrm with kegs of King\u2019s Larger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T16:43:01-07:00","id":1545229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545042-favourite-adversaries?p=1545228#post1545228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you didn\u2019t blast Pentex in the face with magic really. You blasted a fictional versions of Blackwater Security (now known as Triple Canopy Inc. subsidiary of Apollo Global Management with a laundry list of various companies under their management that would make the Pentex board of directors need a change of pants) mercenaries and then celebrated your victory over the Wyrm with kegs of King\u2019s Larger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's something if they did a Curseborne version, I hoped they'd avoid. The whole, &quot;it's like Budweiser only with a very slight sheen of the supernatural.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm entirely comfortable with my fictional entertainment having groups that can actually be destroyed with impunity by my fictional characters.<br /> <br /> Then again, I never thought &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; was an insult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T08:01:05-08:00","id":1545250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545042-favourite-adversaries?p=1545229#post1545229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's something if they did a Curseborne version, I hoped they'd avoid. The whole, &quot;it's like Budweiser only with a very slight sheen of the supernatural.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm entirely comfortable with my fictional entertainment having groups that can actually be destroyed with impunity by my fictional characters.<br /> <br /> Then again, I never thought &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; was an insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of that's an aesthetic issue though, rather than a practical one. <br /> <br /> If your characters can busy into the Headquarters of Pentex and kill their board, then they can also bust into the headquarters of [insert real corporation here] and kill their board. I do appreciate that he concern about getting put on a watch list is probably at least semi-serious (there was, after all, that time Steve Jackson Games got raided by the NSA), but that issue *can* be avoided by doing the &quot;obviously this company but with the serial numbers filed off&quot; thing. <br /> <br /> So the question is then me an aesthetic one. Do you prefer the vibe of a world where you eat McDonalds and drink Coke but there's also the sinister Evilcorp out there doing evil stuff in a way that's curiously unrelated to any of the real companies that exist day to day. Or do you want to be eating O'Donnel's burgers while you watch Daubery Plus on your Peach jPhone only to discover that those three groups are all actually engaging in supernaturally evil business practices.<br /> <br /> More generally I think that big corporate antagonists, much like government agency antagonists, do tend to give the game a particular vibe that can limit individual GMs world building options. Like the Sisters of the Cross work because chances are if you wanted to do religious monster hunters backed by a traditional established church, Catholics backed by the Vatican is almost always what you'd go for so they're a good off the shelf way to fill that niche. <br /> <br /> By contrast there are loads of takes on &quot;sinister corporation&quot; and I don't necessarily want that slot occupied by a Pentex-alike. If nothing else it becomes sort of memeified. If I have sinister corporate shit happening in my game I'd rather the PCs genuinely didn't know who was behind it rather than knowing fit a fact that it was probably The Canon Sinister Corportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T08:41:32-08:00","id":1545253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545042-favourite-adversaries?p=1545250#post1545250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of that's an aesthetic issue though, rather than a practical one.<br /> <br /> If your characters can busy into the Headquarters of Pentex and kill their board, then they can also bust into the headquarters of [insert real corporation here] and kill their board. I do appreciate that he concern about getting put on a watch list is probably at least semi-serious (there was, after all, that time Steve Jackson Games got raided by the NSA), but that issue *can* be avoided by doing the &quot;obviously this company but with the serial numbers filed off&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> So the question is then me an aesthetic one. Do you prefer the vibe of a world where you eat McDonalds and drink Coke but there's also the sinister Evilcorp out there doing evil stuff in a way that's curiously unrelated to any of the real companies that exist day to day. Or do you want to be eating O'Donnel's burgers while you watch Daubery Plus on your Peach jPhone only to discover that those three groups are all actually engaging in supernaturally evil business practices.<br /> <br /> More generally I think that big corporate antagonists, much like government agency antagonists, do tend to give the game a particular vibe that can limit individual GMs world building options. Like the Sisters of the Cross work because chances are if you wanted to do religious monster hunters backed by a traditional established church, Catholics backed by the Vatican is almost always what you'd go for so they're a good off the shelf way to fill that niche.<br /> <br /> By contrast there are loads of takes on &quot;sinister corporation&quot; and I don't necessarily want that slot occupied by a Pentex-alike. If nothing else it becomes sort of memeified. If I have sinister corporate shit happening in my game I'd rather the PCs genuinely didn't know who was behind it rather than knowing fit a fact that it was probably The Canon Sinister Corportation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's a lot to unpack here and the answer is also going to best be summarized is, &quot;What is this game about?&quot;<br /> <br /> CURSEBORNE is a fantastic setting even in just manuscript form but it's going to be appealing to a lot of people who want different things from the game and the big difference is going to be how you choose to express that desire as a Storyteller or player in the greater Curseborne sandbox. Part of why I appreciate this game is it doesn't attempt to shame the &quot;superheroes with claws&quot; form of storytelling and merrily includes Buffy: The Vampire Slayer, Supernatural, and Angel among its inspirations. Which is to say that I could make a Resident Evil adaptation of the game where the player characters decide to go to a secret liminal underground complex of the mad scientist conducting EVIL experiments and blow it up without it being playing &quot;wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, Curseborne seems a lot more Silent Hill (both 1, 2, and 3) over Resident Evil and that's by design but it doesn't mean Resident Evil isn't something that can be done, particularly 4 and 7.<br /> <br /> I should note that in real life, I am well-aware of corporate malfeaseance and the absolute disregard for life that happens. I am someone who saw my particular hometown ravaged by the Sackler Family and the Opiod Crisis and lost friends. Our local chemical plant dumped horrifying amounts of toxins that probably has killed thousands of people in the area. The local steel mill is also a front for the Russian mob and graft to Senator Mitch McConnell as part of a bribe from Putin to him. <a href=\"https://time.com/5651345/rusal-investment-braidy-kentucky/\" target=\"_blank\">No, I'm not making that up.</a><br /> <br /> I don't think there should be a Pentex or Illuminati in the setting but do I think there should be a bunch of evil experiment doing weirdos, creepy weird millionaires doing mad science, and cults of people that are part of massive Multi-Level Marketing schemes that actually spread a mind virus that turns them into members of a Hive Minded spirit. Maybe the company is alive in Curseborne and a living force for evil or maybe you just want to give your bad guys James Bond levels of resources.<br /> <br /> It is an option for play, yes, that the PCs may not be Scooby Doo this time but the Lobby Scene from the Matrix against a cyberpunk company in Silicon Valley that is producing P-Borg out of a plan to TAKE OVER THE WORLD. Its Skynet-esque AI just turns out to be actually a demon from the Outside.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T11:11:07-08:00","id":1545261,"title":"","content":"I think we're mostly on the same page to be honest; I agree sinister corporations are a good fit for the setting but I think they're a good fit for scenario-level or local-level supplements rather than as global antagonists and I think there's a flandersization risk if a specific name corp gets introduced too early.<br /> <br /> I can see a group that's introduced early, even if it's intended as an example or one off villain, evolving into the Pentex of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T17:43:50-08:00","id":1545271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545042-favourite-adversaries?p=1545261#post1545261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're mostly on the same page to be honest; I agree sinister corporations are a good fit for the setting but I think they're a good fit for scenario-level or local-level supplements rather than as global antagonists and I think there's a flandersization risk if a specific name corp gets introduced too early.<br /> <br /> I can see a group that's introduced early, even if it's intended as an example or one off villain, evolving into the Pentex of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could be a middle ground i think, The video game the blackout club takes place in a small suburb town where everyone is employed by a small local company who brainwashes their employees to work on eldritch project underground, everyone is either part of the upper management or completely oblivious to what the company is doing. I could see a campaign starting as newly accursed locals that thanks to their new nature, have been made aware of what is really going on in the town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}